- SpType (spectral type): The luminosity class embedded in spectral type is a key indicator—III indicates giant, II bright giant, IV subgiant, V main-sequence (dwarf). So spectral types with III or II are likely giants.
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants are intrinsically brighter than dwarfs, so Amag is smaller (brighter) for giants. However, in examples, Amag values are somewhat counterintuitive (higher values for dwarfs), likely due to calculation or scale, so must be interpreted carefully.

